  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 936 PM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nA quieter and more comfortable pattern is expected for the latter\nhalf of the week. High temperatures will remain in the mid to\nupper 80s Thursday and Friday under drier air, with only isolated\nor low rain chances. This break provides relief after the active\nand hot start to the week.\n\nTemperatures will gradually warm back into the upper 80s to low\n90s over the weekend and into early next week. There is potential\nfor another shortwave disturbance to bring scattered showers and\nthunderstorms around Friday or Friday night, but confidence in\ncoverage and impacts remain low at this time. Overall, the period\nthrough next Tuesday should feature more seasonal summertime\nconditions with lower risks of widespread severe weather or\nflooding. Diurnal thunderstorm chances may increase again by early\nnext week.",
